cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Arandu in your research, please cite this software and the accompanying article."
title: "Arandu: Open-World Knowledge Graph Construction and Evaluation from Oral Interviews"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/FredDsR/arandu"
url: "https://github.com/FredDsR/arandu"
abstract: >-
  Composable Python pipelines for transcribing oral interviews, generating
  cognitively stratified question-answer benchmarks grounded in Bloom's revised
  taxonomy, constructing knowledge graphs with LLMs, and evaluating retrieval
  strategies via open-world metrics and emic validity.
keywords:
  - knowledge graph construction
  - question answering benchmark
  - oral interviews
  - tacit knowledge elicitation
  - emic validity
  - LLM-as-a-judge
  - retrieval-augmented generation
authors:
